                        "sense_id": "e9a8bec8-d072-378f-bb27-263e6c814265",
                        "entry_id": "e3129bbb-8c8a-3783-9e10-f87099e56e10",
                        "glosses": [
                            "One of various species of grass of the genus Cymbopogon, especially Cymbopogon citratus, which have a lemon-like taste and aroma, and are used in cooking, for tea, and for fragrance."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "uncountable",
                            "usually"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "4613c603-4688-4a03-bb92-6b103011da6a",
                                "sense_id": "e9a8bec8-d072-378f-bb27-263e6c814265",
                                "text": "You could just use ordinary shop-bought kecap manis to marinade the meat, but making your own is easy, has a far more elegant fragrance and is, above all, such a great brag! Flavouring kecap manis is an intensely personal thing, so try this version now and next time cook the sauce down with crushed, split lemongrass and a shredded lime leaf."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
